WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:20.480
<b>TL: Fosky, Ladholyman  Timing, Typesetting: Fosky, JimShew  QC: Maceart, JimShew, Umandsf</b>

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.970
The clock ticks on and on,

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.510
in 60-second cycles.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.750
What do people feel in 60 seconds?

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:29.880
NHK and the 15 animators that best represent Japanese animation present their collaboration.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.000
Ani-Kuri 15. (15 Animation Creators)

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:46.570
Each animator gets 60 seconds to use as they please.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:11.070
What can these 60-second worlds created by the animators let us feel?

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.470
The Hidden Princess

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.270
That's it! That's it!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.500
<b>Princess Tama!</b>

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.610
<b>Chigomaru</b>

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.710
Just a little bit more!

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.120
Princess Tama, your life is ours!

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:25.520
Stop right there!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.540
Okay?

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.000
Yes.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.280
Hidden change!

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.200
Be thankful.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.760
Princess Tama and Chigomaru, with the power of puppetry and the Seal of the Princess,

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.890
can change into Battle Mode in 0.53 seconds.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.520
Oh, no!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.500
Shit, shit!

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.300
<b>Admiral Perori's Ship</b>

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.970
Hidden Princess!

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.710
This is nothing!

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.030
Right back at you!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.340
Take this!

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.230
I've...

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.640
Fallen in love with you.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.450
I love you, Princess Tama.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.570
This tactic...

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.340
does not work on me!

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.440
Why...

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.920
And a new page in history has been opened.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.450
Maybe I went a bit too far...

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.480
Gyrospter

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.130
<b>遥かな 雲の海</b>

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.130
<b>Harukana kumo no umi</b>

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.130
<b>I have been searching for you</b>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.970
<b>あなたを探してる</b>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.970
<b>Anata o sagashiteru</b>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.970
<b>in the sea of clouds, far away.</b>

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:35.490
<b>翼に腕を脱げ</b>

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:35.490
<b>Tsubasa ni ude o nuge</b>

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:35.490
<b>As I turn my arms into wings,</b>

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.590
<b>涙を漂って</b>

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.590
<b>Namida o tadayotte</b>

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.590
<b>my tears fall.</b>

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.490
<b>千年の鳥の声</b>

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.490
<b>Sennen no tori no koe</b>

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.490
<b>With the call of the thousand-year bird,</b>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.760
<b>聞こえるあなたの声が</b>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.760
<b>Kikoeru anata no koe ga</b>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.760
<b>I can hear your voice.</b>

00:03:52.740 --> 00:04:00.860
<b>いつにめぐり合うその今も</b>

00:03:52.740 --> 00:04:00.860
<b>Itsu ni meguriau sono ima mo</b>

00:03:52.740 --> 00:04:00.860
<b>When can the two of us meet in this world?</b>

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:06.120
<b>溶け合う雲の空</b>

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:06.120
<b>Tokeau kumo no sora</b>

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:06.120
<b>The sky is full of clouds.</b>

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.760
<b>あなたを探してみる</b>

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.760
<b>Anata o sagashite miru</b>

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.760
<b>Let me go look for you.</b>

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.390
Amusement Park Kiss

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.370
Beyond the Tears

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.930
<b>ガラスに映った目は</b>

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.930
<b>GARASU ni utsutta me wa</b>

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.930
<b>The eyes reflected on the glass</b>

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.410
<b>思ってた以上にさびてた</b>

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.410
<b>Omotteta ijou ni sabiteta</b>

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.410
<b>are more lonely than I thought.</b>

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.850
<b>視線で交わす言葉は</b>

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.850
<b>Shisen de kawasu kotoba wa</b>

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.850
<b>That glance, which replaced words,</b>

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:50.390
<b>自分でももう分からなくなった</b>

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:50.390
<b>Jibun demo mou wakaranakunatta</b>

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:50.390
<b>even I did understand it anymore.</b>

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.150
<b>どうしよう　笑えるのに</b>

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.150
<b>Doushiyou waraeru noni</b>

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.150
<b>What should I do? I'm smiling,</b>

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.340
<b>涙が止まらない</b>

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.340
<b>Namida ga tomaranai</b>

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.340
<b>but the tears won't stop.</b>

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.320
<b>どうしたの</b>

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.320
<b>Doushitano</b>

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.320
<b>What happened?</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.560
<b>本当は「大丈夫」なんかじゃないよ</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.560
<b>Hontou wa "daijoubu" nanka janaiyo</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.560
<b>I shouldn't have said "It's all right."</b>

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.360
<b>流して　流して</b>

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.360
<b>Nagashite nagashite</b>

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.360
<b>Let them fall, let them fall,</b>

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.830
<b>今この想いを流して</b>

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.830
<b>Ima kono omoi wo nagashite</b>

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.830
<b>just cry my heart out.</b>

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:17.470
<b>明日はそれからでいい</b>

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:17.470
<b>Ashita wa sorekara de ii</b>

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:17.470
<b>Everything will be fine tomorrow.</b>

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:27.530
PROJECT_MERMAID

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.270
Frolicking

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.580
Good Morning

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.000
Good morning.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.240
Sports Colonel Episode 18 - The Assassin Comes to Hunt in the Mountains!!

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:38.960
The colonol hides in the mountains, having barely escaped from his enemy Paul.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.170
<b>大佐</b>

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.170
<b>Taisa</b>

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.170
<b>Colonel.</b>

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.670
<b>鋳物の腕が</b>

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.670
<b>Imono no ude ga</b>

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.670
<b>Your right arm</b>

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:49.800
<b>右に今日もー</b>

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:49.800
<b>Migi ni kyou mo</b>

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:49.800
<b>seems to be in good shape today.</b>

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:54.610
Knowing that Paul will come kill him one day,

00:09:55.370 --> 00:10:01.450
the Colonel realizes that he can't get the kind animals who took care of him involved.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:02.810
Colonel.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:04.200
I'm Wan.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.870
It was a good chance to leave the mountains.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:19.350
The crow and the bear, who were like his own children, chased after him.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:26.040
But they could not save him.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.310
A Gathering of Cats

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:38.650
Meow!

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.450
Oh, you were there? Sorry about that.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:43.870
Oh my, oh my.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:46.940
I'm home, Chobi.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:52.040
Are you that happy to see me home?

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.000
Seconds!

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.050
You're eating too much.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:54.960
What's wrong with Chobi?

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.050
I think he's getting old.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.030
That night...

00:10:59.040 --> 00:10:59.790
Those damn humans!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:00.660
They piss us off!

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:01.750
Let us show them our might!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.330
The battle shall commence tomorrow!

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:18.680
What's wrong with Chobi?

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:19.880
He's getting old.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.180
Oh yeah, Chobi needs to eat, too.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.410
You ate so much!

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.380
The next day

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.380
The battle shall commence tomorrow!

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.300
Alien Invasion - Hiroshi's Circumstances

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.290
Yurururu ~Daily Chapter~

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.750
Start.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:52.000
Fish.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:56.610
Whale.

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:02.950
Whatever.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.450
Bathroom break.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.970
A joke.

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:13.980
Aborted.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.480
Back to work.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.380
PROJECT OMEGA

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.180
No! I'm going to Tokyo!

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:52.840
Breaking news

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:52.840
An UFO is near!?

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:46.650
UFO

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:44.700
Breaking news.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.480
We've just heard from NASA

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:49.470
that a huge UFO is detected on one of their satellites.

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:50.100
LIVE

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:50.100
Satelite Image

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:50.100
NH Conservatory

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:50.720
The crash point is...

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:52.840
Crash Point

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.840
Tokyo... in Shibuya... NHK!?

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.930
Eh!? Isn't that here!?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.930
Emergency... Emergency...

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.330
60 seconds until crash point.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:00.380
Shibuya will be...

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:01.510
There's no other way.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.140
Engage PROJECT OMEGA!

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:06.130
Inputting energy!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.130
Standby for NHK barrier!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.520
Fire!

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:29.580
No way!

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:35.370
Needs... more... power...

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.450
Heat Man

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.300
Attack of Azuma Area #2

00:15:56.840 --> 00:16:01.940
Excuse the interruption. Because of the lack of money, we shall now broadcast simpler images.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.160
Attack of Azuma Area #2

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:23.180
※Invasion Manual

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:23.770
English

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:24.220
Chinese

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:24.590
French

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:25.890
Japanese

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:26.820
Hello?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:33.060
We are from outer space. We are here today to inform you of our invasion.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.220
I don't need it. I don't need anything.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.700
※We may have cut the budget too much.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.060
Sancha Blues

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.610
No way!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:54.200
Wow!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:54.800
Really?

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.110
A murder movie?

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.180
No Way Out.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:16:59.130
You know this album?

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:00.900
Nah.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.210
What should we do next?

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.000
Yeah.

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:03.400
How about there?

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.600
Eh? There again?

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:06.100
Hey, aren't you hungry?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.000
Oh? Isn't this the L'Arc's indie album?

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:13.350
Oh, amazing.

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:14.260
There're so many.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.000
I must collect them.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.130
Oh? X Japan, too.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:19.600
Hello? Midori-chan?

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:23.430
You coming tonight? You left so many drinks here.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.380
Sorry, I'll be right there.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:26.150
Hurry up.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.080
This is the original "Stairway to Heaven!"

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:30.950
Wow, so expensive.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.480
Hey, you got any money?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.030
Still got 200 yen left for this month.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.680
Hey, I have 1,000 yen.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:38.360
Cool!

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.660
This is bad.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.920
The 60-second worlds made by the animation creators...

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:56.420
How did everyone enjoy those 60 seconds?

